    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Result-message failures can count the same usage twice",
      "description": "When `_read_turn` receives an error `ResultMessage` with `accept_error=False`, it folds that result into telemetry and raises. The enclosing `dispatch()` catches the `ProviderError` and replaces its telemetry with `turns.telemetry.snapshot()`, but the normal `collect()` path also folds result messages. In the error path shown, the pre-fold avoids `collect()`, so that particular result is counted once; however, if the same result was already collected during an interrupt drain before the error propagates, it can be folded again. Avoid folding at both the error and collection boundaries, or make result aggregation idempotent.",
